To generate the assert statement based on the given comment, we need to ensure that for every valid index up to the specified index, each element at that index either remains null if it was initially null, or remains unchanged compared to its initial state.

Here's the assert statement in the required format:

<code>assert \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < \old(this.size()); (this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i)));</code>

Explanation:
- `\forall int i; 0 <= i && i < \old(this.size());` ensures that we are considering all valid indices up to the size of the set before the addition.
- `(this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i)))` ensures that for each index `i`, the element either remains null if it was initially null, or remains unchanged compared to its initial state.
--------------------
<code>assert \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < \old(this.size()); (this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i)));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < \old(this.size()); (this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i)));</code>
